        <p>____------ ---- -- Public Notices. THE CORPORATION OF WARRINGTON is prepared to receive LOANS either for eix months' notice or for a term of years. Applications, stating amount for investment, to be made to the Borough Treasurer, Municipal Offices, Warrington.</p>
        <p>LOCAL EXAMINATIONS IN MUSIC. Application is invited for the position of ACTING LOCAL SECRETARY for a Public Local Centre to be formed for Warrington for the Local Examinations of Trinity College of Music. Appli- cants must be resident in Warrington.—Apply to the SECRETARY, Trinity College, London, W. CHESHIRE CONSTABULARY. DEFENCE OF THE REALM. ORDER AS TO LIGHTS. THE following Order, dated 15th December, 1915, made by The Secretary of State, comes into force on 10th January, 1916, and applies to the period from HALF AN HOF • AFTER SUNSET TILL HALF AN HOUR BEFORE SUNRISE:— All lights, whether public or private, which. if unobscured, would be visible from the sea or from the navigable waters of any estuary, must bo extinguished, or, in the case of indoor light, obscured so as to be invisible from outside. Any contravention of this Order is an offence punishable under the defence of the Realm Regulations. WILLIAM LEAH, Acting Chief Constable of Cheshire.</p>
        <p>CHESHIRE CONSTABULARY. DEFENCE OF THE REALM. ORDER AS TO LIGHTS ON VEHICLES. MHE following provisions are contained in an Order dated 15th December, 1915, made by The Secretary of State, which comes into fore._ on 10th January, 1916, in that part of the County of Chester which is situated within six miles of the Sea, or of the navigable, waters of any estuary' and, on the 10th February, 1916, in the remaining portion of the county. PART I. The following provisions apply to the whole of the country:— LIGHTING-UP TIME is altered for all vehicles to between HALF AN HOUR after Sunset and HALF AN HOUR before Sunrise. . VEHICLES DRAWN OR PROPELLED BY HAND.—The requirement to carry ligti •is extended to all vehicles using the road- way, including hand vehicles. RED REAR LIGHTS.—AII vehicles are required to carry a lamp showing a red light to the rear, and a SEPARATE LAMP, CARRIED AT THE REAR, is made compulsory for all except hand vehicles. PART 11. The following provisions apply to that part of the County of Chester situated within six miles of the sea or from the navigable waters of any estuary : The use of HEADLIGHTS of all kinds is PROHIBITED. SIDE-LAMPS are limited as follows: (i.) Front glasses must not exceed six inches across. (ii.) Electric bulbs must not exceed 12 candle power; acetylene burners must not consume more than 14 litres (1- cubic foot) per hour; wicks of oil lamps must not exceed inch in width. (iii.) The front glasses of all electric and acetylene lamps and oil and candle lamps with lens fronts must be ob- scured--electric lamps with at least one thickness of ordinary white tissue paper, acetylene and oil lamps in the same way or with paint, &amp;c., giving similar effect; side panels (except small red and green panels) must be covered over. VEHICLES IN PLACES NEAR THE SEA must not stand in such positions that the lights can.be seen from the Sea. Any offence against this Order is punishable under The Defence of the Realm Regulations. Conies of the Order may be purchased either directly or through any bookseller, from Messrs. Wyman and Sons. Ltd.. 29. Breams Buildings. Fetter-lane, London, E.C. (Price 1(1.) WILLIAM LEAH, Acting Chief Constable of Cheshire.</p>
