        <p>Notices of births, marriages, and deaths, in memoriam notices, and acknowledgments of sympathy are inserted in " The Examiner" at the following rates :—Not exceeding 20 words, 116 each; every additional seven words, 6d.</p>
        <p>Marriages. DALE--JOHNSON.—On the Ist inst., at the Parish Church, by the Rev. Canon Willis, Donald John, son of Mr. and Mrs. Stephen, Dale, of 264, Man- chester-road, to Hilda, daughter of Mr. and Mrs. James Win. Johnson, 294, Manchester-road.</p>
        <p>Deaths. BOYLE.—On January Ist, at 4, Birchall-street, Mary Boyle, aged 72 years. HOLLAND.—On January sth, at 52, Elaine-street; Alfred Holland, aged 65 years. LAWTON.—On January 2nd, at 37, Ashton-street, Mary Ann Lawton, dged 77 years. MAITLAND.--On January 6th, at 26, Livesey-street, Levenslvalme, Helena, the beloved wife of Francis J. Maitland, and daughter, of Mr. and Mrs. E. Place, Stanley-street, Warrington. MASON.—On Friday, January 7th, at 314, Man- chester-road, Catherine, the dear wife of William Mason. MOLLOY.—On January 4th, at 39, Sharp-street, Michael Molloy, aged C. 3 years.</p>
