        <p>Segar Owen, the architect. Later he was in the employ of Messrs. Wright and Hamlin, and for five years previous to the war he was in business on his own account in Golden-square, Warrington. His military career has been fairly extensive. He served four years in the Duke a Lancaster's Yeomanry, and, on the first day of the war, rejoined as a private. He stayed with this regiment for seven months and then was granted a commission in the 4th South Lanca- shire Regiment. An Expert Bomb-Thrower. Going to France last July, he has distin- guished himself on many occasions and is con- sidered an expert at bomb-throwing. During the September advance he was placed in charge TOWN'S CONGRATULATIONS. The Mayor has sent the following message to the officers and men of the 4th South Lanca- shires at the Front:— Mayor's Parlour, Town Hall, Warrington, sth January, 1916. Dear Colonel Fairclough,—Permit Me, on be- half of the borough, to express to you, and</p>
